1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,270
Feels like the rain is about to close in but there's one other place I definitely want to have a look at before I head to the station.
感觉雨就要来了，但去车站之前，还有一个地方我特别想看一看。

2
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:26,400
The ruins of a a norman priory wow I'll tell you what colchester has more than its share of wow moments for a a town of its size.
那就是一座诺曼修道院的遗迹。哇，跟你说，像科尔切斯特这样大小的城镇，让人惊叹的时刻实在不少。

3
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:36,080
Look at this the stunning remains of the priory of st julian and st botolph the first augustinian priory in britain.
看看这个，圣朱利安与圣博托尔夫修道院壮观的遗迹；作者称它是不列颠第一座奥古斯丁修会修道院。

4
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:45,280
Established in 1093 on the site of an older saxon church it remained in use until the english civil war.
作者说它于1093年建在更早的撒克逊教堂旧址上，一直使用到英国内战。

5
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:52,400
Obviously the priory was dissolved at the time of the dissolution of the monasteries in 1536.
当然，修道院在1536年的解散修道院运动期间就已经被解散。

6
00:00:52,400 --> 00:01:00,950
But the site was in use until 1640 what a magical little location.
不过场地一直用到1640年，真是个迷人的小地方。

7
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:07,400
And they reused roman bricks in the building of these incredible pillars here.
他们修建这些惊人的柱子时，还重复利用了罗马砖。

8
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:16,709
Yeah it's such a really imposing impressive site even in its ruined state.
是啊，即使成了废墟，这里仍然很雄伟，很令人赞叹。

9
00:01:16,719 --> 00:01:24,160
You can imagine what it must have looked like in all its pomp and glory in the 11 th and 12 th century.
可以想象，它在十一和十二世纪最辉煌的时候会是什么样子。

10
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:33,870
Well I mean the end of the 11 th but certainly in the 12 th century.
嗯，我指十一世纪末，不过十二世纪肯定是；作者在调整自己说的年代范围。

11
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:40,680
So I think now I'm going to be on my way back to the station starting here at shortwire street.
所以我想，现在该往车站回去了，从这里的 Shortwire Street 出发；街名按来源字幕待核。

12
00:01:40,680 --> 00:02:01,039
That's interesting so this is scheregate colchester's only surviving medieval gate.
有意思，这里是 Scheregate，作者说它是科尔切斯特唯一幸存的中世纪城门。

13
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:09,110
I'll put the meaning of what it means in anglo saxon word I think it means a gap or a notch.
我会把这个盎格鲁撒克逊词的意思写出来；我想它的意思是缺口或凹口。

14
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:23,470
Fantastic I didn't know this was here.
太棒了，我之前还不知道这里有这个。

15
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:35,750
So this is a modern pathway called st john's wind and it crosses over the roman ditch that was outside the city wall.
这是一条叫 St John's Wind 的现代步道，跨过了以前位于城墙外的罗马壕沟；专名依字幕待核。

16
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:43,710
Turning now into headgate street which will become north hill.
现在转进 Headgate Street，再往前就会接到 North Hill。

17
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:49,630
The marquis of granby pub there looks like a fine old timber framed building.
那边的 Marquis of Granby 酒馆，看起来是幢漂亮的老木框架建筑。

18
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:54,909
Who knows could be mock but I don't think so it's nice and warped.
谁知道呢，也许是仿古的，不过我不这么认为；它弯曲得很有味道。

19
00:02:54,919 --> 00:03:03,070
And here are some wonderful timber framed buildings on the banks of the river colne right on the bridge.
河 Colne 岸边还有一些很漂亮的木框架房屋，就在桥上。

20
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:13,110
And I will return to colchester to walk the colne and do the essex serpent walk walk it out towards the sea I'll do that this summer.
我会再来科尔切斯特，沿 Colne 河走，走 Essex Serpent 路线，一路朝海边去；我打算这个夏天走。

21
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:24,230
We're uh leaving the city now so I would say that concludes my very kind of brief walk through some of the incredible history of colchester.
我们现在正离开城市；我想这就结束了这次简短的步行，走过科尔切斯特一些不可思议的历史。

22
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:29,320
I'm really beguiled by colchester I had a wonderful time at the arts centre doing a talk there.
科尔切斯特很让我着迷，我在艺术中心做讲座也度过了愉快的时光。

23
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:37,160
Thank you so much to the people at the arts centre to everyone that came to that talk that was a really special kind of memory for me that.
非常感谢艺术中心的工作人员，以及来听讲座的每一个人，那会是我很特别的一段回忆。

24
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:41,270
And I know there's so much more to colchester than what I've covered in this video.
我知道，科尔切斯特还有很多，远不止这个视频里讲到的这些。

25
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:46,400
But um yeah it's been a long day it's time to go home time to go home so thank you so much for joining me on that walk.
不过今天很长，该回家了，回家了。非常感谢你们陪我走这一路。
